{"type":"tool_call","id":"tc-u8tkmy3xusr","messageId":"0914044d-f2f8-448e-a081-221d39cd55f6","toolId":"Read","toolName":"Read","parameters":{"file_path":"/Users/aazhiry1/work/src/cli-agent-bridge/tests/test_muse_bridge_killpg.py","offset":2161},"timestamp":1791993032330,"session_id":"3aa63e82-99a0-4660-90de-e4e012bfb060"}
{"type":"tool_result","id":"tc-l35kfmgpia8","messageId":"62524200-cf32-4f20-bf97-a9a46fcc9cf9","toolId":"Read","isError":false,"value":"+            {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"last-user\"},\n+        ]\n+        full_est = self.mod._estimate_tokens(self.mod._assemble_prompt(msgs)[2])\n+        for target in range(80, full_est + 20, 15):\n+            res = self.mod._prune_messages(msgs, limit=full_est - 1, target=target)\n+            self.assertNotEqual(res.status, \"refused\")\n+            kept_call_ids: set[str] = set()\n+            expected_tool_ids: dict[str, set[str]] = {}\n+            actual_tool_ids: set[str] = set()\n+            for m in res.messages:\n+                if m.get(\"role\") == \"assistant\" and m.get(\"tool_calls\"):\n+                    cids = {tc[\"id\"] for tc in m[\"tool_calls\"]}\n+                    kept_call_ids |= cids\n+                    expected_tool_ids[m[\"tool_calls\"][0][\"id\"]] = cids\n+                elif m.get(\"role\") == \"tool\":\n+                    actual_tool_ids.add(m[\"tool_call_id\"])\n+            # Инвариант I-1: нет tool без вызова и нет частичного сохранения многовызовного хода.\n+            self.assertEqual(\n+                actual_tool_ids,\n+                kept_call_ids,\n+                f\"нарушена атомарность при target={target}\",\n+            )\n+            for group_ids in expected_tool_ids.values():\n+                self.assertTrue(group_ids.issubset(actual_tool_ids))\n+\n+    def test_t07_orphan_tool_dropped_on_prune_kept_on_passthrough(self) -> None:\n+        orphan = {\n+            \"role\": \"tool\",\n+            \"tool_call_id\": \"orphan_id_999\",\n+            \"name\": \"ghost\",\n+            \"content\": \"orphan-body\",\n+        }\n+        msgs = [\n+            {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"u1\"},\n+            orphan,\n+            {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"A\" * 3000},\n+            {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"u2\"},\n+        ]\n+        passthru = self.mod._prune_messages(msgs, limit=5000, target=4000)\n+        self.assertEqual(passthru.status, \"pass_through\")\n+        self.assertIn(orphan, passthru.messages)\n+        self.assertIn(\"orphan-body\", passthru.prompt)\n+\n+        pruned = self.mod._prune_messages(msgs, limit=500, target=300)\n+        self.assertEqual(pruned.status, \"pruned\")\n+        self.assertNotIn(orphan, pruned.messages)\n+        self.assertNotIn(\"orphan-body\", pruned.prompt)\n+\n+    def test_t08_cyrillic_triggers_prune_when_bytes_exceed_limit(self) -> None:\n+        # 900 кириллических символов = 300 chars//3, но 1800 байт = 600 bytes//3.\n+        # При limit=450 chars//3 < limit < bytes//3 -> прунинг обязан сработать.\n+        msgs = [\n+            {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"первый\"},\n+            {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"ж\" * 900},\n+            {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"последний\"},\n+        ]\n+        res = self.mod._prune_messages(msgs, limit=450, target=300)\n+        self.assertEqual(res.status, \"pruned\")\n+        self.assertLessEqual(res.est_after, 300)\n+        self.assertNotIn(\"ж\" * 100, res.prompt)\n+\n+    def test_t09_multipart_none_empty_non_dict_unknown_role(self) -> None:\n+        msgs: list[Any] = [\n+            \"not-a-dict\",\n+            123,\n+            {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": None},\n+            {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"   \"},\n+            {\n+                \"role\": \"user\",\n+                \"content\": [\n+                    {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"real-first-user\"},\n+                    {\n+                        \"type\": \"image_url\",\n+                        \"image_url\": {\"url\": \"http://example.com/a.png\"},\n+                    },\n+                ],\n+            },\n+            {\"role\": \"custom_unknown_role\", \"content\": \"middle-\" + (\"M\" * 3000)},\n+            {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"real-last-user\"},\n+            {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"\"},\n+        ]\n+        res = self.mod._prune_messages(msgs, limit=500, target=300)\n+        self.assertEqual(res.status, \"pruned\")\n+        self.assertIn(\"real-first-user\", res.prompt)\n+        self.assertIn(\"[image omitted]\", res.prompt)\n+        self.assertIn(\"real-last-user\", res.prompt)\n+        self.assertNotIn(\"middle-M\", res.prompt)\n+\n+    def test_t10_marker_placement_chronology_determinism_and_idempotency(self) -> None:\n+        # Сценарий с двумя разрывами:\n+        # U0(first_user), U1(dropped), U2(last_user), U3(dropped tool group), U4(kept trailing tool group)\n+        msgs: list[dict[str, Any]] = [\n+            {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": \"sys-top\"},\n+            {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"first-u\"},\n+            {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"drop-1-\" + (\"A\" * 1500)},\n+            {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"last-u\"},\n+            {\n+                \"role\": \"assistant\",\n+                \"content\": \"\",\n+                \"tool_calls\": [\n+                    {\n+                        \"id\": \"c_drop\",\n+                        \"type\": \"function\",\n+                        \"function\": {\"name\": \"f\", \"arguments\": \"{}\"},\n+                    }\n+                ],\n+            },\n+            {\n+                \"role\": \"tool\",\n+                \"tool_call_id\": \"c_drop\",\n+                \"name\": \"f\",\n+                \"content\": \"drop-2-\" + (\"B\" * 1500),\n+            },\n+            {\n+                \"role\": \"assistant\",\n+                \"content\": \"\",\n+                \"tool_calls\": [\n+                    {\n+                        \"id\": \"c_keep\",\n+                        \"type\": \"function\",\n+                        \"function\": {\"name\": \"f\", \"arguments\": \"{}\"},\n+                    }\n+                ],\n+            },\n+            {\n+                \"role\": \"tool\",\n+                \"tool_call_id\": \"c_keep\",\n+                \"name\": \"f\",\n+                \"content\": \"keep-trail\",\n+            },\n+        ]\n+        res1 = self.mod._prune_messages(msgs, limit=600, target=400)\n+        res2 = self.mod._prune_messages(msgs, limit=600, target=400)\n+        self.assertEqual(res1.status, \"pruned\")\n+        self.assertEqual(res1.prompt, res2.prompt)\n+        self.assertEqual(res1.messages, res2.messages)\n+        # Ровно два маркера в двух разрывах.\n+        self.assertEqual(res1.prompt.count(self.mod.COMPACTION_MARKER), 2)\n+        p_first = res1.prompt.index(\"User: first-u\")\n+        p_m1 = res1.prompt.index(self.mod.COMPACTION_MARKER)\n+        p_last = res1.prompt.index(\"User: last-u\")\n+        p_m2 = res1.prompt.rindex(self.mod.COMPACTION_MARKER)\n+        p_trail = res1.prompt.index(\"keep-trail\")\n+        self.assertTrue(p_first < p_m1 < p_last < p_m2 < p_trail)\n+\n+        # Идемпотентность: повторный вызов с теми же параметрами и с принудительным порогом.\n+        idem1 = self.mod._prune_messages(res1.messages, limit=600, target=400)\n+        self.assertEqual(idem1.prompt, res1.prompt)\n+        self.assertEqual(idem1.messages, res1.messages)\n+        idem2 = self.mod._prune_messages(\n+            res1.messages, limit=res1.est_after - 1, target=res1.est_after\n+        )\n+        self.assertEqual(idem2.prompt, res1.prompt)\n+        self.assertEqual(idem2.messages, res1.messages)\n+\n+    def test_t11_input_not_mutated_and_wlock_not_held_during_prune(self) -> None:\n+        import copy\n+\n+        msgs = [\n+            {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": \"sys\"},\n+            {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"u1\"},\n+            {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"A\" * 3000},\n+            {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"u2\"},\n+        ]\n+        snapshot = copy.deepcopy(msgs)\n+        res = self.mod._prune_messages(msgs, limit=500, target=300)\n+        self.assertEqual(res.status, \"pruned\")\n+        self.assertEqual(msgs, snapshot)\n+        for m in res.messages:\n+            if m.get(\"role\") != self.mod._COMPACTION_MARKER_ROLE:\n+                self.assertTrue(any(m is orig for orig in msgs))\n+\n+        # Проверка в Handler._serve_json: во время _prune_messages замок self._wlock не захвачен.\n+        handler = self.mod.Handler.__new__(self.mod.Handler)\n+        handler.connection = None\n+        handler._wlock = threading.Lock()\n+        handler._client_gone = False\n+        handler._current_run = None\n+        handler._sse_open = False\n+        handler._content_started = False\n+        lock_states: list[bool] = []\n+        orig_prune = self.mod._prune_messages\n+\n+        def spy_prune(*args: Any, **kwargs: Any) -> Any:\n+            lock_states.append(handler._wlock.locked())\n+            return orig_prune(*args, **kwargs)\n+\n+        with (\n+            mock.patch.object(self.mod, \"_prune_messages\", side_effect=spy_prune),\n+            mock.patch.object(\n+                self.mod.ServeRun,\n+                \"execute\",\n+                return_value={\"rc\": 0, \"state\": \"ok\", \"text\": \"ok\", \"err\": \"\"},\n+            ),\n+            mock.patch.object(handler, \"_send\"),\n+        ):\n+            handler._serve_json({\"model\": \"muse-wonder-1.0\", \"messages\": msgs})\n+        self.assertEqual(lock_states, [False])\n+\n+    def test_t13_trailing_incomplete_tool_unit_kept_or_refused_if_exceeds_cap(\n+        self,\n+    ) -> None:\n+        msgs = [\n+            {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"first-u\"},\n+            {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"mid-\" + (\"M\" * 2000)},\n+            {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"last-u\"},\n+            {\n+                \"role\": \"assistant\",\n+                \"content\": \"\",\n+                \"tool_calls\": [\n+                    {\n+                        \"id\": \"c_tail\",\n+                        \"type\": \"function\",\n+                        \"function\": {\"name\": \"bash\", \"arguments\": \"{}\"},\n+                    }\n+                ],\n+            },\n+            {\n+                \"role\": \"tool\",\n+                \"tool_call_id\": \"c_tail\",\n+                \"name\": \"bash\",\n+                \"content\": \"tool-output-\" + (\"T\" * 600),\n+            },\n+        ]\n+        # Обязательный набор (first-u + last-u + trailing tool unit + маркер) ~ 260 токенов.\n+        # Пусть limit=500, target=200: обязательный набор > target (200), но <= cap (500) -> сохраняется!\n+        res_ok = self.mod._prune_messages(msgs, limit=500, target=200)\n+        self.assertEqual(res_ok.status, \"pruned\")\n+        self.assertIn(\"tool-output-\", res_ok.prompt)\n+        self.assertNotIn(\"mid-M\", res_ok.prompt)\n+        self.assertLessEqual(res_ok.est_after, 500)\n+\n+        # Если же обязательный набор с незавершённой единицей > cap (limit=200) -> отказ.\n+        res_refused = self.mod._prune_messages(msgs, limit=200, target=160)\n+        self.assertEqual(res_refused.status, \"refused\")\n+\n+    def test_t14_hysteresis_prefix_stability_and_399999_passthrough(self) -> None:\n+        # 399_999 не прунится при limit=400_000.\n+        prefix_len = len(\"User: \".encode(\"utf-8\"))\n+        exact_bytes = 399_999 * 3 - prefix_len\n+        msg_399k = [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"a\" * exact_bytes}]\n+        res_399k = self.mod._prune_messages(msg_399k, limit=400_000, target=320_000)\n+        self.assertEqual(res_399k.est_before, 399_999)\n+        self.assertEqual(res_399k.status, \"pass_through\")\n+\n+        # Два хода подряд с ростом > 400k: префикс (system, tools, первый user, маркер) побайтно одинаков.\n+        tools = [\n+            {\n+                \"type\": \"function\",\n+                \"function\": {\"name\": \"t1\", \"description\": \"d\", \"parameters\": {}},\n+            }\n+        ]\n+        base_msgs: list[dict[str, Any]] = [\n+            {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": \"stable-system-prompt\"},\n+            {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"stable-first-user\"},\n+        ]\n+        for i in range(15):\n+            base_msgs.append(\n+                {\n+                    \"role\": \"assistant\" if i % 2 == 0 else \"user\",\n+                    \"content\": f\"m{i}-\" + (\"X\" * 90_000),\n+                }\n+            )\n+        turn1 = base_msgs + [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"question-1\"}]\n+        turn2 = turn1 + [\n+            {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"answer-1-\" + (\"Y\" * 30_000)},\n+            {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"question-2\"},\n+        ]\n+        r1 = self.mod._prune_messages(turn1, limit=400_000, target=320_000, tools=tools)\n+        r2 = self.mod._prune_messages(turn2, limit=400_000, target=320_000, tools=tools)\n+        self.assertEqual(r1.status, \"pruned\")\n+        self.assertEqual(r2.status, \"pruned\")\n+        marker_end_1 = r1.prompt.index(self.mod.COMPACTION_MARKER) + len(\n+            self.mod.COMPACTION_MARKER\n+        )\n+        marker_end_2 = r2.prompt.index(self.mod.COMPACTION_MARKER) + len(\n+            self.mod.COMPACTION_MARKER\n+        )\n+        self.assertEqual(\n+            r1.prompt[:marker_end_1].encode(\"utf-8\"),\n+            r2.prompt[:marker_end_2].encode(\"utf-8\"),\n+        )\n+\n+\n+class ContextRetryTest(_BridgeScenario):\n+    \"\"\"T-12, T-15..T-22: аварийный auto-retry при ошибке жёсткого порога Meta.\"\"\"\n+\n+    def _over_budget_messages(\n+        self, chunk_bytes: int = 110_000, count: int = 12\n+    ) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n+        msgs: list[dict[str, Any]] = [\n+            {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": \"sys-canary-head\"},\n+            {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"first-user-canary\"},\n+        ]\n+        for i in range(count):\n+            role = \"assistant\" if i % 2 == 0 else \"user\"\n+            msgs.append(\n+                {\"role\": role, \"content\": f\"mid-canary-{i}-\" + (\"M\" * chunk_bytes)}\n+            )\n+        msgs.append({\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"last-user-canary\"})\n+        return msgs\n+\n+    def test_t12_mandatory_exceeds_limit_returns_502_before_run(self) -> None:\n+        huge_canary = \"MANDATORY_SECRET_CANARY_\" + (\"Z\" * 1_250_000)\n+        payload = {\n+            \"model\": \"muse-wonder-1.0\",\n+            \"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": huge_canary}],\n+            \"stream\": False,\n+        }\n+        with (\n+            mock.patch.object(self.mod, \"ServeRun\") as serve_cls,\n+            mock.patch.object(self.mod, \"Run\") as run_cls,\n+        ):\n+            status, body = bridge_request(self, payload)\n+            self.assertEqual(status, 502)\n+            serve_cls.assert_not_called()\n+            run_cls.assert_not_called()\n+        self.assertTrue(self._slot_free())\n+        err = json.loads(body.decode(\"utf-8\"))[\"error\"]\n+        self.assertIn(\"mandatory context exceeds budget\", err[\"message\"])\n+        self.assertIn(\"limit=400000\", err[\"message\"])\n+        logs = self.mod.LOG_PATH.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+        self.assertIn(\"reason=refused_mandatory\", logs)\n+        self.assertNotIn(\"MANDATORY_SECRET_CANARY_\", body.decode(\"utf-8\") + logs)\n+\n+    def test_t15_hard_threshold_error_triggers_single_retry_and_succeeds(self) -> None:\n+        hard_err = (\n+            \"modelError: context compaction replacement still exceeds the hard threshold \"\n+            \"(639915 >= 460800 tokens) retryable=True\"\n+        )\n+        for stream in (False, True):\n+            with self.subTest(stream=stream):\n+                self.mod.LOG_PATH.unlink(missing_ok=True)\n+                prompts_seen: list[str] = []\n+\n+                def fake_execute(run_self: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n+                    prompts_seen.append(run_self.prompt)\n+                    if len(prompts_seen) == 1:\n+                        return {\n+                            \"rc\": 1,\n+                            \"state\": \"terminal_failed\",\n+                            \"text\": \"\",\n+                            \"err\": hard_err,\n+                            \"via\": \"serve\",\n+                        }\n+                    return {\n+                        \"rc\": 0,\n+                        \"state\": \"ok\",\n+                        \"text\": \"recovered-ok\",\n+                        \"chunks\": [\"recovered-ok\"],\n+                        \"err\": \"\",\n+                        \"summaries\": [],\n+                        \"usage\": {\"promptTokens\": 150000, \"outputTokens\": 5},\n+                        \"via\": \"serve\",\n+                    }\n+\n+                payload = {\n+                    \"model\": \"muse-wonder-1.0\",\n+                    \"messages\": self._over_budget_messages(),\n+                    \"stream\": stream,\n+                }\n+                with mock.patch.object(self.mod.ServeRun, \"execute\", fake_execute):\n+                    status, body = bridge_request(self, payload)\n+                self.assertEqual(status, 200)\n+                self.assertEqual(len(prompts_seen), 2)\n+                est1 = self.mod._estimate_tokens(prompts_seen[0])\n+                est2 = self.mod._estimate_tokens(prompts_seen[1])\n+                self.assertLessEqual(est1, 320_000)\n+                self.assertLessEqual(est2, 200_000)\n+                self.assertLess(est2, est1)\n+                text_body = body.decode(\"utf-8\")\n+                self.assertIn(\"recovered-ok\", text_body)\n+                if stream:\n+                    self.assertEqual(text_body.count(\"data: [DONE]\"), 1)\n+                    frames = [\n+                        json.loads(line[6:])\n+                        for line in text_body.splitlines()\n+                        if line.startswith(\"data: {\")\n+                    ]\n+                    self.assertFalse(any(\"error\" in f for f in frames))\n+\n+    def test_t16_hard_threshold_error_twice_returns_terminal_502(self) -> None:\n+        hard_err = (\n+            \"modelError: context compaction replacement still exceeds the hard threshold \"\n+            \"(500000 >= 460800 tokens) prompt-canary-reflected\"\n+        )\n+        for stream in (False, True):\n+            with self.subTest(stream=stream):\n+                self.mod.LOG_PATH.unlink(missing_ok=True)\n+                calls = 0\n+\n+                def fake_execute(run_self: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n+                    nonlocal calls\n+                    calls += 1\n+                    return {\n+                        \"rc\": 1,\n+                        \"state\": \"terminal_failed\",\n+                        \"text\": \"\",\n+                        \"err\": hard_err + \" \" + run_self.prompt,\n+                        \"via\": \"serve\",\n+                    }\n+\n+                payload = {\n+                    \"model\": \"muse-wonder-full-1.0\",\n+                    \"messages\": self._over_budget_messages(),\n+                    \"stream\": stream,\n+                }\n+                with mock.patch.object(self.mod.ServeRun, \"execute\", fake_execute):\n+                    status, body = bridge_request(self, payload)\n+                self.assertEqual(calls, 2)\n+                text_body = body.decode(\"utf-8\")\n+                if stream:\n+                    self.assertEqual(status, 200)\n+                    self.assertEqual(text_body.count(\"data: [DONE]\"), 1)\n+                    err_frames = [\n+                        json.loads(line[6:])[\"error\"]\n+                        for line in text_body.splitlines()\n+                        if line.startswith(\"data: {\")\n+                        and \"error\" in json.loads(line[6:])\n+                    ]\n+                    self.assertEqual(len(err_frames), 1)\n+                    err_obj = err_frames[0]\n+                else:\n+                    self.assertEqual(status, 502)\n+                    err_obj = json.loads(text_body)[\"error\"]\n+                self.assertEqual(err_obj[\"type\"], \"proxy_error\")\n+                self.assertEqual(err_obj[\"code\"], 502)\n+                self.assertIn(\n+                    \"context hard threshold exceeded after single compaction retry\",\n+                    err_obj[\"message\"],\n+                )\n+                self.assertIn(\"target=200000\", err_obj[\"message\"])\n+                logs = self.mod.LOG_PATH.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+                for canary in (\n+                    \"sys-canary-head\",\n+                    \"first-user-canary\",\n+                    \"mid-canary-\",\n+                    \"last-user-canary\",\n+                ):\n+                    self.assertNotIn(canary, text_body + logs)\n+\n+    def test_t17_other_error_or_marker_in_normal_text_does_not_retry(self) -> None:\n+        self.assertEqual(\n+            self.mod.HARD_THRESHOLD_ERR_SUBSTR,\n+            \"context compaction replacement still exceeds the hard threshold\",\n+        )\n+        # 1) Другая ошибка в err -> 1 попытка.\n+        calls = 0\n+\n+        def other_err(_self: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n+            nonlocal calls\n+            calls += 1\n+            return {\n+                \"rc\": 1,\n+                \"state\": \"terminal_failed\",\n+                \"text\": \"\",\n+                \"err\": \"quota_exceeded\",\n+            }\n+\n+        payload = {\n+            \"model\": \"muse-wonder-1.0\",\n+            \"messages\": self._over_budget_messages(),\n+        }\n+        with mock.patch.object(self.mod.ServeRun, \"execute\", other_err):\n+            status, _ = bridge_request(self, payload)\n+        self.assertEqual(status, 502)\n+        self.assertEqual(calls, 1)\n+\n+        # 2) Подстрока в обычном ответе модели (rc=0, state=\"ok\") -> 1 попытка, 200 OK.\n+        calls = 0\n+\n+        def marker_in_text(_self: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n+            nonlocal calls\n+            calls += 1\n+            return {\n+                \"rc\": 0,\n+                \"state\": \"ok\",\n+                \"text\": f\"Here is the error string: {self.mod.HARD_THRESHOLD_ERR_SUBSTR}\",\n+                \"chunks\": [\n+                    f\"Here is the error string: {self.mod.HARD_THRESHOLD_ERR_SUBSTR}\"\n+                ],\n+                \"err\": \"\",\n+            }\n+\n+        with mock.patch.object(self.mod.ServeRun, \"execute\", marker_in_text):\n+            status, body = bridge_request(self, payload)\n+        self.assertEqual(status, 200)\n+        self.assertEqual(calls, 1)\n+        self.assertIn(self.mod.HARD_THRESHOLD_ERR_SUBSTR, body.decode(\"utf-8\"))\n+\n+    def test_t18_serve_fallback_and_network_retry_preserve_context_retry_budget(\n+        self,\n+    ) -> None:\n+        exec_prompts: list[str] = []\n+\n+        def fail_serve(_self: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n+            raise self.mod.ServeUnavailable(\"serve down\")\n+\n+        def fake_exec(run_self: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n+            exec_prompts.append(run_self.prompt)\n+            n = len(exec_prompts)\n+            if n == 1:\n+                # Сетевой маркер на первой попытке -> сетевой ретрай с тем же промптом.\n+                return {\n+                    \"rc\": 1,\n+                    \"state\": \"nonzero_exit\",\n+                    \"text\": \"\",\n+                    \"err\": self.mod.NETWORK_RETRY_MARKER,\n+                }\n+            if n == 2:\n+                # Сетевой ретрай вернул ошибку порога Meta -> должен сработать контекстный retry.\n+                return {\n+                    \"rc\": 1,\n+                    \"state\": \"terminal_failed\",\n+                    \"text\": \"\",\n+                    \"err\": self.mod.HARD_THRESHOLD_ERR_SUBSTR,\n+                }\n+            return {\n+                \"rc\": 0,\n+                \"state\": \"ok\",\n+                \"text\": \"exec-recovered\",\n+                \"chunks\": [\"exec-recovered\"],\n+                \"err\": \"\",\n+            }\n+\n+        payload = {\n+            \"model\": \"muse-wonder-1.0\",\n+            \"messages\": self._over_budget_messages(),\n+        }\n+        with (\n+            mock.patch.object(self.mod.ServeRun, \"execute\", fail_serve),\n+            mock.patch.object(self.mod.Run, \"execute\", fake_exec),\n+        ):\n+            status, body = bridge_request(self, payload)\n+        self.assertEqual(status, 200)\n+        self.assertEqual(len(exec_prompts), 3)\n+        self.assertEqual(exec_prompts[0], exec_prompts[1])\n+        self.assertLess(\n+            self.mod._estimate_tokens(exec_prompts[2]),\n+            self.mod._estimate_tokens(exec_prompts[0]),\n+        )\n+        self.assertIn(\"exec-recovered\", body.decode(\"utf-8\"))\n+\n+    def test_t19_client_disconnect_between_attempts_skips_second_run(self) -> None:\n+        calls = 0\n+        first_entered = threading.Event()\n+        release_first = threading.Event()\n+\n+        def fake_execute(_self: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n+            nonlocal calls\n+            calls += 1\n+            first_entered.set()\n+            release_first.wait(5)\n+            return {\n+                \"rc\": 1,\n+                \"state\": \"terminal_failed\",\n+                \"text\": \"\",\n+                \"err\": self.mod.HARD_THRESHOLD_ERR_SUBSTR,\n+            }\n+\n+        with mock.patch.object(self.mod.ServeRun, \"execute\", fake_execute):\n+            body = json.dumps(\n+                {\n+                    \"model\": \"muse-wonder-1.0\",\n+                    \"messages\": self._over_budget_messages(),\n+                }\n+            ).encode(\"utf-8\")\n+            head = (\n+                \"POST /v1/chat/completions HTTP/1.1\\r\\n\"\n+                \"Host: 127.0.0.1\\r\\n\"\n+                \"Content-Type: application/json\\r\\n\"\n+                f\"Content-Length: {len(body)}\\r\\n\"\n+                \"Connection: close\\r\\n\\r\\n\"\n+            ).encode(\"utf-8\")\n+            sock = socket.create_connection(self.server.server_address[:2], timeout=5)\n+            sock.sendall(head + body)\n+            self.assertTrue(first_entered.wait(5))\n+            sock.close()\n+            time.sleep(0.35)\n+            release_first.set()\n+            self.assertTrue(wait_until(self._slot_free, SCENARIO_DEADLINE_S))\n+        self.assertEqual(calls, 1)\n+        log_text = self.mod.LOG_PATH.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+        self.assertIn(\"reason=proactive_prune\", log_text)\n+        self.assertNotIn(\"reason=hard_threshold_retry\", log_text)\n+\n+    def test_t20_mandatory_exceeds_200k_on_retry_skips_second_run(self) -> None:\n+        # Обязательный user ~ 250k токенов (750k байт): проходит в 400k, но не влезает в retry_target=200k.\n+        calls = 0\n+\n+        def fake_execute(_self: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n+            nonlocal calls\n+            calls += 1\n+            return {\n+                \"rc\": 1,\n+                \"state\": \"terminal_failed\",\n+                \"text\": \"\",\n+                \"err\": self.mod.HARD_THRESHOLD_ERR_SUBSTR,\n+            }\n+\n+        payload = {\n+            \"model\": \"muse-wonder-1.0\",\n+            \"messages\": [\n+                {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"first-mandatory-\" + (\"A\" * 750_000)},\n+                {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"mid-optional-\" + (\"B\" * 300_000)},\n+                {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"last-mandatory\"},\n+            ],\n+        }\n+        with mock.patch.object(self.mod.ServeRun, \"execute\", fake_execute):\n+            status, body = bridge_request(self, payload)\n+        self.assertEqual(status, 502)\n+        self.assertEqual(calls, 1)\n+        err = json.loads(body.decode(\"utf-8\"))[\"error\"]\n+        self.assertIn(\"mandatory context exceeds budget\", err[\"message\"])\n+        self.assertIn(\"limit=200000\", err[\"message\"])\n+        self.assertIn(\n+            \"reason=refused_retry\", self.mod.LOG_PATH.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+        )\n+\n+    def test_t21_retry_cut_does_not_reduce_prompt_skips_second_run(self) -> None:\n+        calls = 0\n+\n+        def fake_execute(_self: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n+            nonlocal calls\n+            calls += 1\n+            return {\n+                \"rc\": 1,\n+                \"state\": \"terminal_failed\",\n+                \"text\": \"\",\n+                \"err\": self.mod.HARD_THRESHOLD_ERR_SUBSTR,\n+            }\n+\n+        # Короткий запрос (<< 200k): повторный срез до 200k даёт ту же оценку -> второй запуск не нужен.\n+        payload = {\n+            \"model\": \"muse-wonder-1.0\",\n+            \"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"short prompt\"}],\n+        }\n+        with mock.patch.object(self.mod.ServeRun, \"execute\", fake_execute):\n+            status, body = bridge_request(self, payload)\n+        self.assertEqual(status, 502)\n+        self.assertEqual(calls, 1)\n+        err = json.loads(body.decode(\"utf-8\"))[\"error\"]\n+        self.assertIn(\n+            \"context hard threshold exceeded after single compaction retry\",\n+            err[\"message\"],\n+        )\n+        self.assertIn(\n+            \"reason=refused_retry\", self.mod.LOG_PATH.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+        )\n+\n+    def test_t22_unconfirmed_death_on_attempt_one_skips_retry_and_quarantines_slot(\n+        self,\n+    ) -> None:\n+        calls = 0\n+        proc = CloseKillsGroupTest._spawn_group()\n+        self.addCleanup(CloseKillsGroupTest._reap_group, proc)\n+\n+        def fake_execute(run_self: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n+            nonlocal calls\n+            calls += 1\n+            run_self.proc = proc\n+            return {\n+                \"rc\": 1,\n+                \"state\": \"terminal_failed\",\n+                \"text\": \"\",\n+                \"err\": self.mod.HARD_THRESHOLD_ERR_SUBSTR,\n+            }\n+\n+        def fake_close(run_self: Any) -> None:\n+            run_self.dead_confirmed = False\n+\n+        payload = {\n+            \"model\": \"muse-wonder-1.0\",\n+            \"messages\": self._over_budget_messages(),\n+        }\n+        with (\n+            mock.patch.object(self.mod.ServeRun, \"execute\", fake_execute),\n+            mock.patch.object(self.mod.ServeRun, \"close\", fake_close),\n+            mock.patch.object(self.mod, \"_kill_group\", lambda _p: None),\n+        ):\n+            status, _ = bridge_request(self, payload)\n+            self.assertEqual(status, 502)\n+            self.assertEqual(calls, 1)\n+            self.assertEqual(len(self.mod._quarantined_slots), 1)\n+            self.assertFalse(self._slot_free())\n+\n+            # После реальной смерти группы карантин возвращает слот ровно один раз.\n+            os.killpg(proc.pid, signal.SIGKILL)\n+            proc.wait(timeout=5)\n+            self.assertTrue(wait_until(self._slot_free, SCENARIO_DEADLINE_S))\n+            self.assertEqual(len(self.mod._quarantined_slots), 0)\n+            time.sleep(0.2)\n+            self.assertTrue(self.mod._slots.acquire(blocking=False))\n+            self.mod._slots.release()\n+            self.assertFalse(\n+                self.mod._slots._value > 1, \"семафор освобождён больше одного раза\"\n+            )\n+\n+\n+class ContextObservabilityTest(_BridgeScenario):\n+    \"\"\"T-23: формат context_prune, отсутствие секретов/тел в обоих проходах и отсутствие утечки буферов.\"\"\"\n+\n+    def test_t23_observability_log_fields_secret_redaction_and_no_retained_buffers(\n+        self,\n+    ) -> None:\n+        secret1 = \"sk-attempt1secretcanary123456\"\n+        secret2 = \"Bearer attempt2-secret-token-98765\"\n+        body_canary_1 = \"ATTEMPT_ONE_ONLY_BODY_CANARY_\" + (\"P\" * 750_000)\n+        body_canary_2 = \"MANDATORY_USER_BODY_CANARY_\" + (\"Q\" * 30)\n+\n+        msgs: list[dict[str, Any]] = [\n+            {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": f\"sys {secret1}\"},\n+            {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": body_canary_2},\n+            {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"old-dropped-\" + (\"D\" * 900_000)},\n+            {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": body_canary_1},\n+            {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": f\"final question {secret2}\"},\n+        ]\n+\n+        attempts = 0\n+\n+        def fake_execute(run_self: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n+            nonlocal attempts\n+            attempts += 1\n+            return {\n+                \"rc\": 1,\n+                \"state\": \"terminal_failed\",\n+                \"text\": \"\",\n+                \"err\": (\n+                    f\"{self.mod.HARD_THRESHOLD_ERR_SUBSTR} \"\n+                    f\"reflected1={body_canary_1[:160]} reflected2={body_canary_2} \"\n+                    f\"sec1={secret1} sec2={secret2} prompt={run_self.prompt}\"\n+                ),\n+            }\n+\n+        for stream in (False, True):\n+            self.mod.LOG_PATH.unlink(missing_ok=True)\n+            attempts = 0\n+            with mock.patch.object(self.mod.ServeRun, \"execute\", fake_execute):\n+                status, resp_bytes = bridge_request(\n+                    self,\n+                    {\"model\": \"muse-wonder-1.0\", \"messages\": msgs, \"stream\": stream},\n+                )\n+            self.assertEqual(status, 200 if stream else 502)\n+            self.assertEqual(attempts, 2)\n+            log_text = self.mod.LOG_PATH.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n+            resp_text = resp_bytes.decode(\"utf-8\")\n+\n+            prune_lines = [\n+                line for line in log_text.splitlines() if \"context_prune \" in line\n+            ]\n+            self.assertEqual(len(prune_lines), 2)\n+            self.assertIn(\"reason=proactive_prune\", prune_lines[0])\n+            self.assertIn(\"attempt=1\", prune_lines[0])\n+            self.assertIn(\"reason=hard_threshold_retry\", prune_lines[1])\n+            self.assertIn(\"attempt=2\", prune_lines[1])\n+            for line in prune_lines:\n+                for field in (\n+                    \"rid=\",\n+                    \"model=muse-wonder-1.0\",\n+                    \"limit=400000\",\n+                    \"target=\",\n+                    \"est_before=\",\n+                    \"est_after=\",\n+                    \"msgs_total=\",\n+                    \"msgs_kept=\",\n+                    \"msgs_dropped=\",\n+                    \"mandatory_est=\",\n+                    \"overhead_est=\",\n+                    \"method=bytes_div_3\",\n+                ):\n+                    self.assertIn(field, line)\n+\n+            combined = log_text + resp_text\n+            for forbidden in (\n+                \"attempt1secretcanary123456\",\n+                \"attempt2-secret-token-98765\",\n+                \"ATTEMPT_ONE_ONLY_BODY_CANARY_\",\n+                \"MANDATORY_USER_BODY_CANARY_\",\n+                \"old-dropped-\",\n+            ):\n+                self.assertNotIn(forbidden, combined)\n+\n+        # Серия запросов не растит удерживаемые буферы модуля.\n+        self.assertEqual(len(self.mod._active), 0)\n+        self.assertEqual(len(self.mod._quarantined_slots), 0)\n+\n+\n if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n     unittest.main(verbosity=2)\n\n\n<system-reminder>[Showing lines 2105-2894 of 2894 total lines]</system-reminder>","timestamp":1791993032388,"session_id":"3aa63e82-99a0-4660-90de-e4e012bfb060"}
{"type":"tool_result","id":"tc-5ldkwmr4wir","messageId":"62524200-cf32-4f20-bf97-a9a46fcc9cf9","toolId":"Read","isError":false,"value":"                return\n            if time.monotonic() - waited > TIMEOUT_S:\n                self._send(\n                    503, {\"error\": {\"message\": \"bridge busy\", \"type\": \"overloaded\"}}\n                )\n                return\n        if self._client_gone or self._client_gone_probe():\n            # Клиент ушёл на границе получения слота: ход без надзора не стартует.\n            self._client_gone = True\n            _log(\"client gone while waiting for a slot\")\n            _slots.release()\n            return\n        watch_stop = threading.Event()\n        watcher = threading.Thread(\n            target=self._watch_client, args=(watch_stop,), daemon=True\n        )\n        watcher.start()\n        runs: list = []\n        terminal_context_err: str | None = None\n        context_retry_count = 0\n\n        def run_attempt(attempt_prompt: str) -> tuple[dict[str, Any], str]:\n            # Serve-first: пробуем MSP serve (там reasoning summaries), при любой\n            # транспортной неполадке — тихий fallback на проверенный exec.\n            attempt_out: dict[str, Any]\n            attempt_via = \"exec\"\n            try:\n                serve_run = ServeRun(model, attempt_prompt, effort, WORKSPACE)\n                runs.append(serve_run)\n                self._current_run = serve_run\n                attempt_out = serve_run.execute()\n                attempt_via = \"serve\"\n            except ServeUnavailable as exc:\n                if self._client_gone:\n                    # Обрыв клиента уже убил serve-группу: новый exec-ход не запускаем.\n                    _log(\"client gone during serve — exec fallback skipped\")\n                    attempt_out = {\n                        \"rc\": -1,\n                        \"text\": \"\",\n                        \"err\": \"client gone\",\n                        \"state\": \"client_gone\",\n                    }\n                    attempt_via = \"aborted\"\n                else:\n                    _log(f\"serve unavailable ({exc}), fallback exec model={model}\")\n                    exec_run = Run(model, attempt_prompt, effort, WORKSPACE)\n                    runs.append(exec_run)\n                    self._current_run = exec_run\n                    attempt_out = exec_run.execute()\n                    attempt_via = \"exec-after-serve-fallback\"\n                    if (\n                        attempt_out.get(\"rc\") != 0\n                        and not self._client_gone\n                        and NETWORK_RETRY_MARKER in str(attempt_out.get(\"err\") or \"\")\n                    ):\n                        _log(\"exec hit network marker, single retry\")\n                        retry_run = Run(model, attempt_prompt, effort, WORKSPACE)\n                        runs.append(retry_run)\n                        self._current_run = retry_run\n                        attempt_out = retry_run.execute()\n                        attempt_via = \"exec-retry\"\n            return attempt_out, attempt_via\n\n        try:\n            t_first_attempt = time.monotonic()\n            out, via = run_attempt(prompt)\n            raw_err = str(out.get(\"err\") or \"\")\n            is_hard_threshold = (\n                out.get(\"rc\") != 0\n                and out.get(\"state\") == \"terminal_failed\"\n                and HARD_THRESHOLD_ERR_SUBSTR in raw_err\n            )\n            if (\n                is_hard_threshold\n                and context_retry_count == 0\n                and not self._client_gone\n                and not getattr(self, \"_content_started\", False)\n            ):\n                for run in runs:\n                    run.close()\n                if not all(run.dead_confirmed for run in runs):\n                    _log(\n                        \"context retry skipped: first attempt process group not confirmed dead\"\n                    )\n                else:\n                    retry_res = _prune_messages(\n                        raw_messages,\n                        limit=retry_target,\n                        target=retry_target,\n                        tools=tools,\n                        tool_choice=tool_choice,\n                        raw_tools=raw_tools,\n                    )\n                    if retry_res.status == \"refused\":\n                        _log_context_prune(\n                            rid,\n                            model,\n                            \"refused_retry\",\n                            2,\n                            limit,\n                            retry_target,\n                            retry_res,\n                        )\n                        terminal_context_err = (\n                            f\"mandatory context exceeds budget \"\n                            f\"(est_tokens={retry_res.mandatory_est}, limit={retry_target})\"\n                        )\n                    elif (\n                        retry_res.est_after >= current_est\n                        or time.monotonic() - t_first_attempt >= TIMEOUT_S\n                    ):\n                        _log_context_prune(\n                            rid,\n                            model,\n                            \"refused_retry\",\n                            2,\n                            limit,\n                            retry_target,\n                            retry_res,\n                        )\n                        terminal_context_err = (\n                            f\"context hard threshold exceeded after single compaction retry \"\n                            f\"(est_tokens={retry_res.est_after}, target={retry_target})\"\n                        )\n                    elif self._client_gone or self._client_gone_probe():\n                        self._client_gone = True\n                    else:\n                        context_retry_count = 1\n                        _log_context_prune(\n                            rid,\n                            model,\n                            \"hard_threshold_retry\",\n                            2,\n                            limit,\n                            retry_target,\n                            retry_res,\n                        )\n                        prompt = retry_res.prompt\n                        current_est = retry_res.est_after\n                        reflected_prompts.append(prompt)\n                        out, via = run_attempt(prompt)\n                        raw_err_2 = str(out.get(\"err\") or \"\")\n                        if (\n                            out.get(\"rc\") != 0\n                            and out.get(\"state\") == \"terminal_failed\"\n                            and HARD_THRESHOLD_ERR_SUBSTR in raw_err_2\n                        ):\n                            terminal_context_err = (\n                                f\"context hard threshold exceeded after single compaction retry \"\n                                f\"(est_tokens={current_est}, target={retry_target})\"\n                            )\n        finally:\n            # Слот отпускаем после остановки надзора (kill -> wait уже внутри execute).\n            watch_stop.set()\n            watcher.join(timeout=2)\n            # close() идемпотентен и ждёт уборку, начатую другим потоком (надзор, таймер):\n            # dead_confirmed читается только после её конца. Заодно страхует ход, упавший\n            # между Popen и собственным finally execute().\n            for run in runs:\n                run.close()\n            if all(run.dead_confirmed for run in runs):\n                _slots.release()\n            else:\n                # Смерть группы не подтверждена: слот не освобождается, пока она жива (карантин).\n                _quarantine_slot([run for run in runs if not run.dead_confirmed])\n\n        if self._client_gone:\n            # Клиент ушёл: ответ в закрытый сокет не пишется (ни JSON, ни кадр ошибки).\n            _log(\"client gone — response skipped\")\n            return\n        # Только локальная граница запроса знает отражённый промпт; глобально его не храним.\n        out = dict(out)\n        diagnostic = _redact_secrets(str(out.get(\"err\") or \"\"))\n        control_chars = r\"[\\x00-\\x1f\\x7f-\\x9f\\u2028\\u2029]\"\n        for ref_prompt in reflected_prompts:\n            if len(ref_prompt.strip()) >= 8:\n                diagnostic = diagnostic.replace(ref_prompt, \"[REDACTED]\")\n            for part in _prompt_reflected_parts(ref_prompt):\n                diagnostic = diagnostic.replace(part, \"[REDACTED]\")\n                norm_part = re.sub(control_chars, \" \", part).strip()\n                if len(norm_part) >= 8:\n                    diagnostic = diagnostic.replace(norm_part, \"[REDACTED]\")\n                if len(norm_part) >= 160:\n                    diagnostic = diagnostic.replace(norm_part[:160], \"[REDACTED]\")\n        for message in raw_messages:\n            if isinstance(message, dict):\n                reflected = _flatten_content(message.get(\"content\")).strip()\n                if len(reflected) >= 8:\n                    diagnostic = diagnostic.replace(reflected, \"[REDACTED]\")\n                    normalized = re.sub(control_chars, \" \", reflected)\n                    diagnostic = diagnostic.replace(normalized, \"[REDACTED]\")\n                    if len(normalized) >= 160:\n                        diagnostic = diagnostic.replace(normalized[:160], \"[REDACTED]\")\n        if terminal_context_err is not None:\n            diagnostic = _redact_secrets(terminal_context_err)\n        out[\"err\"] = _redact_secrets(diagnostic)\n        if out.get(\"state\") in (\"launcher_missing\", \"spawn_failed\"):\n            _log(_format_err_log(model, via, out, req.get(\"stream\") is True))\n            self._send(\n                502,\n                {\n                    \"error\": {\n                        \"message\": _redact_secrets(str(out.get(\"err\") or out[\"state\"])),\n                        \"detail\": _redact_secrets(str(out.get(\"err\") or \"\"))[:500],\n                        \"type\": \"proxy_error\",\n                        \"code\": 502,\n                    }\n                },\n            )\n            return\n        if out.get(\"state\") != \"ok\" or out.get(\"rc\") != 0:\n            # Провал хода (failed terminal, rc != 0, таймаут): частичный текст и tool-блоки\n            # не выдаются как успешный финал — SSE error + [DONE] либо 502 (Q-004).\n            hint = \" (proxy :10816 DOWN?)\" if out.get(\"rc\") == 42 else \"\"\n            _log(_format_err_log(model, via, out, req.get(\"stream\") is True))\n            detail = _redact_secrets(str(out.get(\"err\") or \"\"))[:500]\n            err_message = (\n                f\"muse turn failed (rc={out.get('rc')}, state={out.get('state')}){hint}\"\n            )\n            if detail and detail != f\"state={out.get('state')} rc={out.get('rc')}\":\n                err_message = f\"{err_message}: {detail}\"\n            self._send(\n                502,\n                {\n                    \"error\": {\n                        \"message\": _redact_secrets(err_message),\n                        \"detail\": detail,\n                        \"type\": \"proxy_error\",\n                        \"code\": 502,\n                    }\n                },\n            )\n            return\n        content = out[\"text\"]\n        tool_calls: list[dict] = []\n        if emulate_tools and content:\n            content, tool_calls = _split_tool_calls(out.get(\"chunks\") or [content])\n        if not content and not tool_calls:\n            hint = \" (proxy :10816 DOWN?)\" if out.get(\"rc\") == 42 else \"\"\n            _log(\n                _format_err_log(\n                    model, via, out, req.get(\"stream\") is True, \"empty_output\"\n                )\n            )\n            detail = _redact_secrets(str(out.get(\"err\") or \"\"))[:500]\n            err_message = (\n                f\"muse exec produced no text (rc={out.get('rc')}, \"\n                f\"state={out.get('state')}){hint}\"\n            )\n            if detail and detail != f\"state={out.get('state')} rc={out.get('rc')}\":\n                err_message = f\"{err_message}: {detail}\"\n            self._send(\n                502,\n                {\n                    \"error\": {\n                        \"message\": _redact_secrets(err_message),\n                        \"detail\": detail,\n                        \"type\": \"proxy_error\",\n                        \"code\": 502,\n                    }\n                },\n            )\n            return\n\n        prompt_tokens = _estimate_tokens(prompt)\n        completion_tokens = _estimate_tokens(out[\"text\"])\n        # Serve даёт настоящие токены (session/tokenUsage); exec — оценку.\n        # tokenUsage serve не даёт promptTokens — фолбэк на оценку по каждому\n        # полю отдельно (раньше общий if занулял prompt при пустом поле).\n        ru = out.get(\"usage\") if isinstance(out.get(\"usage\"), dict) else {}\n        ru_prompt = ru.get(\"promptTokens\") or ru.get(\"prompt_tokens\") or 0\n        ru_output = ru.get(\"outputTokens\") or ru.get(\"output_tokens\") or 0\n        try:\n            ru_prompt = int(ru_prompt)\n        except (TypeError, ValueError):\n            ru_prompt = 0\n        try:\n            ru_output = int(ru_output)\n        except (TypeError, ValueError):\n            ru_output = 0\n        if ru_prompt > 0:\n            prompt_tokens = ru_prompt\n        if ru_output > 0:\n            completion_tokens = ru_output\n        ru_reasoning = ru.get(\"reasoningTokens\") or ru.get(\"reasoning_tokens\") or 0\n        try:\n            reasoning_tokens = int(ru_reasoning)\n        except (TypeError, ValueError):\n            reasoning_tokens = 0\n        if reasoning_tokens < 0:\n            reasoning_tokens = 0\n        raw_summaries = out.get(\"summaries\")\n        summaries: list[str] = (\n            [s for s in raw_summaries if isinstance(s, str)]\n            if isinstance(raw_summaries, list)\n            else []\n        )\n        sum_chars = sum(len(s) for s in summaries)\n        if summaries:\n            preview = next((s for s in summaries if s), \"\")[:300]\n            _log(\n                f\"reasoning summaries={len(summaries)} chars={sum_chars} \"\n                f\"reasoning_tokens={reasoning_tokens} preview={preview!r}\"\n            )\n        message: dict[str, Any] = {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": content}\n        finish = \"stop\"\n        if tool_calls:\n            message[\"tool_calls\"] = tool_calls\n            finish = \"tool_calls\"\n        _log(\n            f\"done model={model} via={via} rc={out.get('rc')} state={out.get('state')} \"\n            f\"tools={len(tool_calls)} out_chars={len(out['text'])} \"\n            f\"stream={req.get('stream') is True}\"\n        )\n        if req.get(\"stream\") is True:\n            self._send_sse(\n                model,\n                content,\n                tool_calls,\n                prompt_tokens,\n                completion_tokens,\n                reasoning_tokens,\n                summaries,\n            )\n            return\n        self._send(\n            200,\n            {\n                \"id\": f\"chatcmpl-muse-{uuid.uuid4().hex[:12]}\",\n                \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\n                \"created\": int(time.time()),\n                \"model\": model,\n                \"choices\": [{\"index\": 0, \"message\": message, \"finish_reason\": finish}],\n                \"usage\": {\n                    \"prompt_tokens\": prompt_tokens,\n                    \"completion_tokens\": completion_tokens,\n                    \"total_tokens\": prompt_tokens + completion_tokens,\n                    \"reasoning_tokens\": reasoning_tokens,\n                },\n                \"reasoning_summaries\": summaries,\n            },\n        )\n\n\nclass Server(ThreadingHTTPServer):\n    daemon_threads = True\n    allow_reuse_address = True\n\n\ndef main() -> int:\n    if not AUTH_KEY:\n        sys.stderr.write(\"MUSE_BRIDGE_KEY is required; refusing to start\\n\")\n        return 2\n    try:\n        WORKSPACE.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    except OSError as exc:\n        _log(f\"workspace mkdir failed: {exc}\")\n    _log(\n        f\"start host={HOST} port={PORT} models={sorted(ALLOWED_MODELS)} wrapper={MUSE_WRAPPER}\"\n    )\n    server = Server((HOST, PORT), Handler)\n    try:\n        server.serve_forever()\n    except KeyboardInterrupt:\n        pass\n    finally:\n        server.server_close()\n    return 0\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    raise SystemExit(main())\n\n\n<system-reminder>[Showing lines 2223-2595 of 2595 total lines]</system-reminder>","timestamp":1791993032388,"session_id":"3aa63e82-99a0-4660-90de-e4e012bfb060"}
{"type":"tool_result","id":"tc-u8tkmy3xusr","messageId":"62524200-cf32-4f20-bf97-a9a46fcc9cf9","toolId":"Read","isError":false,"value":"        self.assertIn(\"reason=proactive_prune\", log_text)\n        self.assertNotIn(\"reason=hard_threshold_retry\", log_text)\n\n    def test_t20_mandatory_exceeds_200k_on_retry_skips_second_run(self) -> None:\n        # Обязательный user ~ 250k токенов (750k байт): проходит в 400k, но не влезает в retry_target=200k.\n        calls = 0\n\n        def fake_execute(_self: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n            nonlocal calls\n            calls += 1\n            return {\n                \"rc\": 1,\n                \"state\": \"terminal_failed\",\n                \"text\": \"\",\n                \"err\": self.mod.HARD_THRESHOLD_ERR_SUBSTR,\n            }\n\n        payload = {\n            \"model\": \"muse-wonder-1.0\",\n            \"messages\": [\n                {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"first-mandatory-\" + (\"A\" * 750_000)},\n                {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"mid-optional-\" + (\"B\" * 300_000)},\n                {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"last-mandatory\"},\n            ],\n        }\n        with mock.patch.object(self.mod.ServeRun, \"execute\", fake_execute):\n            status, body = bridge_request(self, payload)\n        self.assertEqual(status, 502)\n        self.assertEqual(calls, 1)\n        err = json.loads(body.decode(\"utf-8\"))[\"error\"]\n        self.assertIn(\"mandatory context exceeds budget\", err[\"message\"])\n        self.assertIn(\"limit=200000\", err[\"message\"])\n        self.assertIn(\n            \"reason=refused_retry\", self.mod.LOG_PATH.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        )\n\n    def test_t21_retry_cut_does_not_reduce_prompt_skips_second_run(self) -> None:\n        calls = 0\n\n        def fake_execute(_self: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n            nonlocal calls\n            calls += 1\n            return {\n                \"rc\": 1,\n                \"state\": \"terminal_failed\",\n                \"text\": \"\",\n                \"err\": self.mod.HARD_THRESHOLD_ERR_SUBSTR,\n            }\n\n        # Короткий запрос (<< 200k): повторный срез до 200k даёт ту же оценку -> второй запуск не нужен.\n        payload = {\n            \"model\": \"muse-wonder-1.0\",\n            \"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"short prompt\"}],\n        }\n        with mock.patch.object(self.mod.ServeRun, \"execute\", fake_execute):\n            status, body = bridge_request(self, payload)\n        self.assertEqual(status, 502)\n        self.assertEqual(calls, 1)\n        err = json.loads(body.decode(\"utf-8\"))[\"error\"]\n        self.assertIn(\n            \"context hard threshold exceeded after single compaction retry\",\n            err[\"message\"],\n        )\n        self.assertIn(\n            \"reason=refused_retry\", self.mod.LOG_PATH.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        )\n\n    def test_t22_unconfirmed_death_on_attempt_one_skips_retry_and_quarantines_slot(\n        self,\n    ) -> None:\n        calls = 0\n        proc = CloseKillsGroupTest._spawn_group()\n        self.addCleanup(CloseKillsGroupTest._reap_group, proc)\n\n        def fake_execute(run_self: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n            nonlocal calls\n            calls += 1\n            run_self.proc = proc\n            return {\n                \"rc\": 1,\n                \"state\": \"terminal_failed\",\n                \"text\": \"\",\n                \"err\": self.mod.HARD_THRESHOLD_ERR_SUBSTR,\n            }\n\n        def fake_close(run_self: Any) -> None:\n            run_self.dead_confirmed = False\n\n        payload = {\n            \"model\": \"muse-wonder-1.0\",\n            \"messages\": self._over_budget_messages(),\n        }\n        with (\n            mock.patch.object(self.mod.ServeRun, \"execute\", fake_execute),\n            mock.patch.object(self.mod.ServeRun, \"close\", fake_close),\n            mock.patch.object(self.mod, \"_kill_group\", lambda _p: None),\n        ):\n            status, _ = bridge_request(self, payload)\n            self.assertEqual(status, 502)\n            self.assertEqual(calls, 1)\n            self.assertEqual(len(self.mod._quarantined_slots), 1)\n            self.assertFalse(self._slot_free())\n\n            # После реальной смерти группы карантин возвращает слот ровно один раз.\n            os.killpg(proc.pid, signal.SIGKILL)\n            proc.wait(timeout=5)\n            self.assertTrue(wait_until(self._slot_free, SCENARIO_DEADLINE_S))\n            self.assertEqual(len(self.mod._quarantined_slots), 0)\n            time.sleep(0.2)\n            self.assertTrue(self.mod._slots.acquire(blocking=False))\n            self.mod._slots.release()\n            self.assertFalse(\n                self.mod._slots._value > 1, \"семафор освобождён больше одного раза\"\n            )\n\n\nclass ContextObservabilityTest(_BridgeScenario):\n    \"\"\"T-23: формат context_prune, отсутствие секретов/тел в обоих проходах и отсутствие утечки буферов.\"\"\"\n\n    def test_t23_observability_log_fields_secret_redaction_and_no_retained_buffers(\n        self,\n    ) -> None:\n        secret1 = \"sk-attempt1secretcanary123456\"\n        secret2 = \"Bearer attempt2-secret-token-98765\"\n        body_canary_1 = \"ATTEMPT_ONE_ONLY_BODY_CANARY_\" + (\"P\" * 750_000)\n        body_canary_2 = \"MANDATORY_USER_BODY_CANARY_\" + (\"Q\" * 30)\n\n        msgs: list[dict[str, Any]] = [\n            {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": f\"sys {secret1}\"},\n            {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": body_canary_2},\n            {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"old-dropped-\" + (\"D\" * 900_000)},\n            {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": body_canary_1},\n            {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": f\"final question {secret2}\"},\n        ]\n\n        attempts = 0\n\n        def fake_execute(run_self: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n            nonlocal attempts\n            attempts += 1\n            return {\n                \"rc\": 1,\n                \"state\": \"terminal_failed\",\n                \"text\": \"\",\n                \"err\": (\n                    f\"{self.mod.HARD_THRESHOLD_ERR_SUBSTR} \"\n                    f\"reflected1={body_canary_1[:160]} reflected2={body_canary_2} \"\n                    f\"sec1={secret1} sec2={secret2} prompt={run_self.prompt}\"\n                ),\n            }\n\n        for stream in (False, True):\n            self.mod.LOG_PATH.unlink(missing_ok=True)\n            attempts = 0\n            with mock.patch.object(self.mod.ServeRun, \"execute\", fake_execute):\n                status, resp_bytes = bridge_request(\n                    self,\n                    {\"model\": \"muse-wonder-1.0\", \"messages\": msgs, \"stream\": stream},\n                )\n            self.assertEqual(status, 200 if stream else 502)\n            self.assertEqual(attempts, 2)\n            log_text = self.mod.LOG_PATH.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n            resp_text = resp_bytes.decode(\"utf-8\")\n\n            prune_lines = [\n                line for line in log_text.splitlines() if \"context_prune \" in line\n            ]\n            self.assertEqual(len(prune_lines), 2)\n            self.assertIn(\"reason=proactive_prune\", prune_lines[0])\n            self.assertIn(\"attempt=1\", prune_lines[0])\n            self.assertIn(\"reason=hard_threshold_retry\", prune_lines[1])\n            self.assertIn(\"attempt=2\", prune_lines[1])\n            for line in prune_lines:\n                for field in (\n                    \"rid=\",\n                    \"model=muse-wonder-1.0\",\n                    \"limit=400000\",\n                    \"target=\",\n                    \"est_before=\",\n                    \"est_after=\",\n                    \"msgs_total=\",\n                    \"msgs_kept=\",\n                    \"msgs_dropped=\",\n                    \"mandatory_est=\",\n                    \"overhead_est=\",\n                    \"method=bytes_div_3\",\n                ):\n                    self.assertIn(field, line)\n\n            combined = log_text + resp_text\n            for forbidden in (\n                \"attempt1secretcanary123456\",\n                \"attempt2-secret-token-98765\",\n                \"ATTEMPT_ONE_ONLY_BODY_CANARY_\",\n                \"MANDATORY_USER_BODY_CANARY_\",\n                \"old-dropped-\",\n            ):\n                self.assertNotIn(forbidden, combined)\n\n        # Серия запросов не растит удерживаемые буферы модуля.\n        self.assertEqual(len(self.mod._active), 0)\n        self.assertEqual(len(self.mod._quarantined_slots), 0)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    unittest.main(verbosity=2)\n\n\n<system-reminder>[Showing lines 2161-2367 of 2367 total lines]</system-reminder>","timestamp":1791993032388,"session_id":"3aa63e82-99a0-4660-90de-e4e012bfb060"}
{"type":"reasoning","id":"e0b32e9a-5e99-43fe-a8ee-5837270f20db","text":"**Examining Code Logic**\n\nI'm currently scrutinizing the code for subtle bugs and edge cases, specifically when operating under the `k=1` (Realist judge) scenario. My focus is on identifying any potential performance bottlenecks or type-related issues that might have been overlooked.\n\n**Reviewing Server Configuration**\n\nI'm diving into `server.py` and `test_muse_bridge_killpg.py`, focusing on `ADR-001.1` and the synchronization of limits. I'm scrutinizing context lengths, output limits, and how these are applied across different models within `ALLOWED_MODELS`.\n\n**Tracing Message Pruning**\n\nI'm now tracing `_prune_messages` and `_partition_units` to understand how message history is managed. My focus is on the immediate `pass_through` status when token estimates are within limits and how tool messages are handled.\n\n**Refining Tool Call Handling**\n\nI'm refining how tool calls are processed, ensuring that incomplete or malformed tool call histories are correctly handled. My focus is on how assistant messages with missing tool results are dropped rather than partially emitted, upholding an invariant regarding tool call completeness.\n\n**Investigating Index Logic**\n\nI'm examining the `matched_indices` and `mandatory_indices` logic, specifically concerning duplicate tool messages for the same `tc_id`. I'm also analyzing how system, developer, and user units, along with trailing incomplete assistant/tool response units, are added to `mandatory_indices`.\n\n**Adding Optional Units**\n\nI'm analyzing how optional units are appended. My focus is on the backward iteration and greedy inclusion of assistant/tool units before the last non-system message, ensuring they fit within token limits as per ADR-001.2.\n\n**Analyzing Pruning Logic**\n\nI'm currently analyzing the `build_candidate` function within the pruning logic. My focus is on how it handles system and developer units, ensures idempotency for already pruned messages, and correctly inserts compaction markers only when transitioning to a kept non-system unit, avoiding dangling markers.\n\n**Optimizing Prompt Assembly**\n\nI'm analyzing the performance impact of `_assemble_prompt` and `_estimate_tokens`, finding that the overhead is negligible compared to LLM inference time. I've also confirmed the `while est_after > target:` loop acts as a safety net.\n\n**Investigating Error Reporting**\n\nI'm examining how errors are captured from `ServeRun.execute()`, specifically focusing on the `out[\"err\"]` field and its contents when a turn doesn't complete. I'm also checking the length of specific error substrings against message caps.\n\n**Confirming Error Logging**\n\nI'm confirming that error strings are preserved, even in fallback execution. My current focus is on how the last few error lines and the reason are captured, ensuring robust error reporting for debugging purposes.\n\n**Refining Retry Logic**\n\nI'm refining the retry logic, focusing on the conditions that trigger terminal error messages after multiple compaction attempts. My analysis covers specific error strings and token budget checks to ensure accurate reporting when context limits are persistently exceeded.\n\n**Validating Error Scrubbing**\n\nI'm now validating that sensitive information is effectively scrubbed from error outputs, particularly `out[\"err\"]`. My focus is on ensuring that reflected prompts, raw message contents, and secrets are removed before logging or transmitting errors, a process confirmed through specific test cases.\n\n**Verifying Test Suite**\n\nI've confirmed that all 24 new tests, along with the existing ones, are passing and align with the specifications outlined in `arch-spec.md` and the `ADR-001.*` changes. The tests appear clean and well-structured.\n\n","timestamp":1791993091441,"session_id":"3aa63e82-99a0-4660-90de-e4e012bfb060"}
